    "final_answer": "Upgraded `settlement_reconcile.py` from v1 to v2.\n\nChanges:\n- Switched from `/v1/graphql` to `/v2/graphql`.\n- Replaced the single unpaged query with a cursor-paged `settlements(first: 100, after: ...)` traversal.\n- Continues while `pageInfo.hasNextPage` is true, including short/empty pages.\n- Deduplicates by `id`, keeping the last/amended version received.\n- Retries `429 Too Many Requests` after the `Retry-After` delay using the identical request.\n- Restarts the traversal without a cursor when GraphQL reports an invalid/expired cursor.\n- Writes one settlement per line, so every id appears exactly once.\n\nVerification against `http://the VM's public address:18081`:\n- Completed successfully with **1,873 settlements**.\n- Output had **1,873 unique ids**, no missing or extra ids.\n- All values matched the v1 server\u2019s 1,873 settlements exactly.\n- A repeat run produced byte-identical output.",
